request.description:
`PUT /api/releases/draft/{reference}/tracks/{trackRef}/contributors`

Sets the track's contributor credits (producer, composer, mixer…). **Replace-all**: whatever you send becomes the complete list — always send every credit, not just the new one. To remove all credits use **DELETE** on this same URL (an empty array here is a 422 by design). Optional step — the wizard checklist does not require contributors. Draft-only: after submit this answers **409**.

#### Path params

- `:reference` — the draft's reference. e.g. `REL7K2M9QX4TBWH01`
- `:trackRef` — the track's reference. e.g. `TRK4H8N2WQ7XKMV93`

#### Request payload — `application/json`

- `contributors` (array, **required**, 1–50 items) — each item:
  - `name` (string, **required**) — the person's name, 1–255 chars.
  - `role` (string, **required**) — a slug from `GET /api/meta/contributors`, e.g. `producer`, `composer`, `mixer`. Anything not on that list is a 422.

```json
{
  "contributors": [
    { "name": "Young John", "role": "producer" },
    { "name": "Ayra", "role": "composer" }
  ]
}
```

#### Response `data`

- `contributors` (array) — the saved list, `{name, role}` per credit, in the order you sent.

#### Errors

`401` · Not authenticated · `403` · Label staff without `release.edit` · `404` · Release **or track** not found or not yours · `409` · Already submitted · `422` · Validation failed — bad items use dotted keys, e.g. `contributors.1.role` · `429` · Rate limited

```json
{
  "status": false,
  "message": "Validation failed.",
  "errors": {
    "contributors.1.role": "Pick a role from the contributor roles list (/api/meta/contributors)."
  }
}
```

#### Example response — 200

```json
{
  "status": true,
  "message": "Contributors saved.",
  "data": {
    "contributors": [
      { "name": "Young John", "role": "producer" },
      { "name": "Ayra", "role": "composer" }
    ]
  }
}
```

